    "path": "packs/pf2e/actions/heritage/undine/salt-wound.json",
    "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/foundryvtt/pf2e/blob/581c2bf2ca9734f4dd83f034fbcc93f8e4fd96eb/packs/pf2e/actions/heritage/undine/salt-wound.json",
    "sourceBlob": "77cf116e7af3c5751f1eee06a16dcfeabe896d00",
    "description": "<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature that has blood and is not at its maximum Hit Points hits you with a melee Strike</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You channel salt and brine from your blood into the creature's wounds. The creature must attempt a @Check[fortitude|against:class-spell] using your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher. On a failure, the creature takes @Damage[1d6[persistent,acid]] damage and is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Sickened]{Sickened 1} by the pain. On a critical failure, it instead takes @Damage[2d6[persistent,acid]] damage and is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Sickened]{Sickened 2}.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "Frequency once per day Trigger A creature that has blood and is not at its maximum Hit Points hits you with a melee Strike Effect You channel salt and brine from your blood into the creature's wounds. The creature must attempt a fortitude check using your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher. On a failure, the creature takes damage acid damage and is Sickened 1 by the pain. On a critical failure, it instead takes damage acid damage and is Sickened 2.",
